<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#tui-kanokupolu">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuʻi Kanokupolu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tuʻi Kanokupolu is the title of the third and youngest of Tonga's royal lines, founded in the early 17th century by a son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tui-haatakalaua">Tuʻi Haʻatakalaua</a>. Its holders became the effective rulers of Tonga, while the Tuʻi Tonga kept a sacred status. In 1845 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-tupou-i">Tāufaʻāhau</a>, the Tuʻi Kanokupolu, united the islands as King George Tupou I, and the title has since been held by the Tongan monarchy.</p></div>
